From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zygote: Keep seccomp when SELinux is absent

Zygote skips every seccomp filter, for apps, app zygotes, system_server
and the setuid/setgid range, when security_getenforce() is 0, so that
"setenforce 0" also lifts seccomp while debugging. Deckard's libselinux
reports 0 there because SELinux is ignored, not permissive, so every
Android process ran with no Android seccomp filter at all.

Upstream libselinux returns -1 without selinuxfs, which keeps the
filters on. Match that: only a running, permissive SELinux turns
seccomp off.
---
 core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp b/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
index 27220c00e..b11d2d4a9 100644
--- a/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
@@ -2870,8 +2870,9 @@ static void com_android_internal_os_Zygote_nativeInitNativeState(JNIEnv* env, jc
    */
 
   // security_getenforce is not allowed on app process. Initialize and cache
-  // the value before zygote forks.
-  gIsSecurityEnforced = security_getenforce();
+  // the value before zygote forks. Only a permissive SELinux turns seccomp
+  // off; without SELinux the filters stay on.
+  gIsSecurityEnforced = is_selinux_enabled() <= 0 || security_getenforce() != 0;
 
   // Disabled for Deckard
   /*selinux_android_seapp_context_init();*/
